The human gene X has a sequence below ATTGC (second T red); chimpanzee has sequence below ATGGC (first G red); the orangutan (outgroup) has a sequence below of ATGGC (first G red). The point of ancestry for the human and chimpanzee are the same; the node for the orangutan is much lower and has an earlier node, further down. The ancestral node between human and chimpanzee has an image of the blue cylinder labeled Gene X, labeled Ancestor. The sequence below the image is labeled ATGGC, with the first G red. This is shown to be the ancestral gene." id="524" name="Google Shape;524;p73"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="2462212" y="1520825"/><a:ext cx="4548187" cy="5175250"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>